summary: Measure system latency using rtla timerlat.
description: |
  This test measures system latency in microseconds (us) using rtla timerlat.
  It runs the rtla timerlat command in the background using tmux and
  checks if latency exceeds the maximum threshold.

  Use the /start case to start measuring latency as a background process.
  Use the /stop case to stop the background process and report results.

  Inputs:
    - LATENCY_THRES_US: The maximum threshold for acceptable latency in microseconds.
  Expected results:
    - Both start and stop cases should run successfully and the latency should be below the maximum threshold.
contact: Pablo Ridolfi <pridolfi@redhat.com>
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - tmux
  - rtla
duration: 24h
